These ten are my picks. Nearly all are "same-edge" interactions, where the condition says what the edit replaces. Replacing `none` with a 3x3 conv should gain the most, and removing or downgrading an existing 3x3 conv should cost the most. I expect both patterns to hold across all three datasets.

I left out the cross-edge redundancy and chaining hypotheses because their direction is less reliable. I also left out edge 2, where the gain from activating the edge is probably smaller.

{"hypotheses": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv where the direct edge was absent opens a new path, a larger gain than upgrading an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning on edge 5 with a conv adds a route into the output, gaining more than upgrading an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Activating edge 4 with a conv adds a deep path through node 1, a larger gain than swapping ops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 0 gates node 1, so replacing none with conv enables whole paths and gains substantially."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none on edge 1 activates a main route into node 2 and gives a large gain."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on the direct edge costs more accuracy than removing a weak op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on edge 5 loses more capacity than deleting a skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on edge 4 removes a deep high-capacity path, a bigger drop than deleting weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for a parameter-free skip loses learnable capacity, a bigger drop than replacing weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with a skip on edge 5 drops capacity more than replacing weaker ops."}]}
